course: dictionary
lesson: 5456
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Landslide is one of them. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it, which is its context. In a geography lesson, the words around it talk about hills, rain and houses.
explain: «Tsunamis can also be caused by landslides, volcanic eruptions and, very rarely, meteorite impacts.» Here a landslide is a huge mass of earth and rock sliding down a slope, under the sea as well as on land. The word tsunami tells you this is about nature, not elections.
explain: «A landslide is winning by a huge amount; a narrow win is a very close one.» Now the words narrow win and winning tell you the second meaning. In politics, a landslide means one side won by far more votes than the others. You can say win by a landslide or a landslide victory.
fact: A landslide is a large mass of earth, rocks and mud that suddenly slides down a hill or mountain.
fact: Heavy rain, earthquakes and cutting down trees can all cause a landslide.
fact: A landslide can block roads and bury houses, so keep away from steep slopes after storms.
fact: In politics, a landslide means a huge win in an election, with far more votes than the others.
fact: Mount St Helens in the USA erupted in 1980 when its whole north side collapsed in a giant landslide.
exercise: «Tsunamis can also be caused by landslides, volcanic eruptions and, very rarely, meteorite impacts.» What is a landslide in this sentence? | *A mass of earth and rock sliding down a slope | A small pile of sand on a beach | A huge win in an election | A very close vote
exercise: «A landslide is winning by a huge amount; a narrow win is a very close one.» What does landslide mean here? | A heavy storm at sea | *A huge win, by far more votes | A narrow path up a hill | A slope covered in grass
exercise: Which words in «win by a landslide» tell you it is about politics? | win, by, a | a, win | *win, landslide | by, a, landslide
test: «About 8,000 years ago an underwater landslide off Norway, the Storegga Slide, sent a tsunami onto Scotland.» Which thing caused the tsunami? | A volcano | A meteorite | A flood of rain | *A landslide under the sea
test: A news report says, «The party won by a landslide.» What does it mean? | The party lost every vote | The party moved to a new hill | *The party won by far more votes than the others | The party won a very close race
exam: Pick the best meaning and say why: «After heavy rain, a landslide blocked the road to the village.» | A party that rose in the polls | *A mass of earth and rock sliding down, because the rain and the blocked road are about nature | A huge win in an election | A narrow path
